---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_437",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 437,
  "text": "[[1968.1]] <b>359.  Spatium et motus revera relationes [Anfang 1677 (?)]</b>\n [[1968.2]] <tab/>[Anfang 1677 (?)] </p>\n<p> [[1968.6]] Si <b>Spatium</b> sit res quaedam in pura extensione posita, <b>materiae</b> autem natura sit\n[[1968.7]] spatium implere; et <b>Motus</b> est spatii mutatio, tunc motus erit absolutum quoddam, et\n[[1968.8]] duobus corporibus sibi invicem appropinquantibus dici poterit utrum moveatur aut quiescat;\n[[1968.9]] vel, si ambo moventur, quanam moveantur celeritate. Atque inde sequentur eae\n[[1968.10]] conclusiones, quas olim ostendi in <i>Theoria motus abstracte considerati</i>. Sed revera\n[[1968.11]] Spatium illud res non est, neque motus est aliquid absolutum, sed consistit in relatione. Et\n[[1968.12]] proinde si duo corpora sibi concurrant, celeritas inter ipsa ita animo partienda est, ut sibi\n[[1968.13]] occurrere intelligantur eadem vi. Itaque si duo corpora concurrentia intelligantur aequalia,\n[[1968.14]] statim omnia phaenomena experimentis consentanea ex hoc solo deducentur. Assumo\n[[1968.15]] igitur corpora alia esse dura quae post concursum reflectantur, alia mollia quae simul\n[[1968.16]] maneant. Et assero: duo corpora [mollia] aequalia et similia eadem celeritate concurrentia,\n[[1968.17]] post concursum simul manere; dura vero ea qua venere celeritate reflecti.\n[[1968.18]] <petit> </p>\n<p> [[1968.19]] <i>Leibniz ersetzte den Text in Kleindruck zusammen mit der dazugehörigen Zeichnung durch das Folgende\n[[1968.20]] und hat versehentlich nur den auf der Rückseite des Manuskripts stehenden Schluß gestrichen</i>: </p>\n<p> [[1968.21]] His positis sit navis <i>LMN</i> in qua duo corpora aequalia et similia eadem celeritate concurrant; eodem\n[[1968.22]] tempore uno veniente ab <i>L</i> per <i>LM</i> altero ab <i>N</i> per <i>NM</i> ipsi <i>LM</i> aequalem, itaque eadem celeritate reflectentur\n[[1968.23]] contraria autem directione, ut eodem tempore quo ante concursum venerant ab <i>L</i> et <i>N</i> ad <i>M</i>, post concursum\n[[1968.24]] redeant ad <i>L</i> et <i>N</i>, si quidem perfecte elastica sunt, vel simul maneant, in <i>M</i> si mollia. Interea ponatur navis\n[[1969.1]] progredi ab <i>₁L₁M₁N</i> in <i>₂L₂M₂N</i>, quae secum feret\n[[1969.2]] globos in ipsa decurrentes. Sit jam ripa immota\n[[1969.3]] <i>PT</i> in qua punctis <i>₁L₁M₁N</i> respondeant puncta\n[[1969.4]] <i>P.R.Q.</i> et punctis <i>₂L.₂M.₂N</i> puncta <i>S.V.T.</i> </petit> </p>\n<p> [[1969.5]] His positis sit navis <i>LMN</i>, in qua\n[[1969.6]] duo globi aequales et similes <i>A, B</i>, concurrant\n[[1969.7]] uno <i>A</i> veniente a prora <i>L</i> ad\n[[1969.8]] medium <i>M</i>, altero <i>B</i> eodem tempore a\n[[1969.9]] puppi <i>N</i> ad idem medium <i>M</i>, celeritate\n[[1969.10]] proinde aequali, et motu uniformi seu aequabili. In <i>M</i> autem concurrentia haec duo\n[[1969.11]] corpora <i>A</i> et <i>B</i>, si Elastri perfecte capacia sint reflectantur, et aequali tempore ac celeritate\n[[1969.12]] redibunt <i>A</i> quidem ex <i>M</i> in <i>L</i>, at <i>B</i> ex <i>M</i> in <i>N</i>. </p>\n<p> [[1969.13]] Haec dum in navi perinde fiunt, ac si quiesceret, ipsa navis interim motu aequabili\n[[1969.14]] secundo flumine recta deferatur, ita ut navis initio motus globulorum sit in loco <i>₁L₁M₁N</i>,\n[[1969.15]] momento autem concursus sit in loco\n[[1969.16]] <i>₂L₂M₂N</i>, et denique momento absoluti\n[[1969.17]] recursus, seu cum corpora <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> post\n[[1969.18]] concursum ad priora loca sunt reversa,\n[[1969.19]] sit in loco <i>₃L₃M₃N</i>. In ripa autem\n[[1969.20]] immota <i>PY</i> sint puncta respondentia,\n[[1969.21]] nempe <i>PQR</i> ipsis <i>₁L₁M₁N</i>, et <i>STV</i> ipsis\n[[1969.22]] <i>₂L₂M₂N</i>, et <i>XYZ</i> ipsis [<i>₃L₃M₃N</i>]. Patet\n[[1969.23]] absolute loquendo et respectu ripae\n[[1969.24]] immotae perinde esse ac si dicamus\n[[1969.25]] corpora <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> celeritatibus <i>PT</i> et <i>RT</i> concurrentia in <i>T</i> post concursum reflecti celeritatibus\n[[1969.26]] <i>TX</i> et <i>TZ</i>, ubi quidem (si corpora sint aequalia) manifestum est celeritates et\n[[1969.27]] directiones corporum concurrentium permutari, seu <i>TX</i> aequari ipsi <i>RT</i> et <i>TZ</i> ipsi <i>PT</i>. Est\n[[1969.28]] enim <i>TX</i> aequal. <i>₂M₂L</i> seu <i>ML</i>, minus <i>₂L₃L</i> seu <i>XS</i>, seu <i>PS</i>. Et <i>RT</i>, est <i>₁N₁M</i> seu <i>NM</i> seu\n[[1969.29]] <i>ML</i>, minus <i>₁M₂M</i> seu <i>₁L₂L</i> seu <i>PS</i>. Si vero corpora sint mollia post concursum simul\n[[1969.30]] manebunt et cum navi deferentur, ex <i>₂M</i> in <i>₃M</i>. Itaque si duo corpora mollia concurrant\n[[1969.31]] celeritatibus <i>PT</i> et <i>RT</i> post concursum simul ibunt celeritate et directione <i>TY</i>, directione\n[[1970.1]] quidem celerioris, celeritas autem <i>TY</i> seu <i>₂M₃M</i> seu <i>XS</i> erit dimidia differentia celeritatum\n[[1970.2]] <i>PT</i> et <i>RT</i>. Est autem <i>PS</i> aequ. <i>XS</i> seu dimidia <i>PX</i> et <i>PX</i> est <i>PT</i> minus <i>TX</i> seu <i>PT</i> minus\n[[1970.3]] <i>TR</i>. </p>\n",
  "number": "359.",
  "title": "Spatium et motus revera relationes",
  "date": "[Anfang 1677 (?)]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:359. Spatium et motus revera relationes [Anfang 1677 (?)] [Anfang 1677 (?)] Si Spatium sit res quaedam in pura extensione posita, materiae autem natura sit spatium implere; et Motus est spatii mutatio, tunc motus erit absolutum quoddam, et duobus corporibus sibi invicem appropinquantibus dici poteri...">
      <div class="text-content">
        {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
          paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>